{
 "voice": "am_puck",
 "duration": 71.285,
 "lines": [
  {
   "line": 0,
   "text": "What if every billionaire on Earth exploded, and anyone who ever became one exploded too?",
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 5.695
  },
  {
   "line": 1,
   "text": "Right now, there are three thousand four hundred and twenty-eight billionaires, sitting on about twenty trillion dollars.",
   "start": 6.135,
   "end": 12.12
  },
  {
   "line": 2,
   "text": "At noon tomorrow: pop. Pop. Pop.",
   "start": 12.44,
   "end": 14.955
  },
  {
   "line": 3,
   "text": "Pool parties go quiet. Limousines wait outside, forever.",
   "start": 15.315,
   "end": 19.05
  },
  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "But the money doesn't vanish. It goes to their kids.",
   "start": 19.41,
   "end": 22.355
  },
  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "And the moment a kid inherits a billion: pop.",
   "start": 22.595,
   "end": 25.165
  },
  {
   "line": 6,
   "text": "Then the grandkids. Pop, pop.",
   "start": 25.465,
   "end": 27.525
  },
  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "Lawyers start chopping fortunes into pieces as fast as they can.",
   "start": 27.885,
   "end": 31.615
  },
  {
   "line": 8,
   "text": "Luckily, America's biggest lottery winner took the cash option: nine hundred and ninety-seven point six million dollars.",
   "start": 32.015,
   "end": 39.235
  },
  {
   "line": 9,
   "text": "Unluckily, he's one good stock tip away from going pop.",
   "start": 39.555,
   "end": 42.76
  },
  {
   "line": 10,
   "text": "It's hot potato with money. You only blow up if you're holding too much, so you pass it on.",
   "start": 43.24,
   "end": 48.385
  },
  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "Split three billion between four kids, and nobody pops.",
   "start": 48.625,
   "end": 51.73
  },
  {
   "line": 12,
   "text": "So the rich would race to give it away. More than two hundred and fifty of them have already promised to.",
   "start": 52.09,
   "end": 57.74
  },
  {
   "line": 13,
   "text": "But the rule never said which currency.",
   "start": 58.18,
   "end": 60.26
  },
  {
   "line": 14,
   "text": "In two thousand and eight, Zimbabwe's money got so worthless that a loaf of bread cost billions of dollars.",
   "start": 60.58,
   "end": 66.79
  },
  {
   "line": 15,
   "text": "Zimbabwe dollars.",
   "start": 67.03,
   "end": 68.36
  },
  {
   "line": 16,
   "text": "The whole bakery queue would have gone pop.",
   "start": 68.72,
   "end": 70.725
  }
 ],
